@startuml tightness_ranking_and_verify
title Explain tight graphs - ranking (in Solve check) [4] and Verify run [5]

partition "ranking, inside WorldSearch (no extra time) [4]" {
  start
  :failed coarse or refinement attempt arrives
  with its closest state (lowest cost reached);
  :ObstacleFinder: laws that state leaves violated
  - illegal pair touching -> that IllegalPairLaw
  - patch outside its cell range -> its SizeRangeLaw
  - patch short of its required border -> its RequiredBorderLaw
  - biome absent -> MissingBiome
  - patch over perimeter / thickness limit -> ShapeLimit;
  :TightnessTally: +1 per obstacle
  (each counted once per attempt);
  if (search ends UNPROVEN?) then (yes)
    :verdict lists top obstacles:
    "blocked N of M failed attempts"
    labelled as measurement, not proof;
  else (FEASIBLE / INFEASIBLE)
    :no ranking shown;
  endif
  stop
}

partition "Verify run (button, up to 10 min) [5]" {
  start
  :read ranking file written by the last Solve check;
  if (graph fingerprint changed since?) then (yes)
    :fail loud: run the Solve check again;
    stop
  endif
  :arms = baseline graph + one loosened copy per
  top-3 loosenable obstacle
  (pair -> legal, size range -> widened, border -> dropped,
  ShapeLimit / MissingBiome skipped, said so);
  :run production coarse attempts, arms interleaved
  on every thread, until 10 min;
  :per arm: solved k of n, exact confidence range;
  :arm "improves" only if its low bound
  is above the baseline's high bound;
  :report table: baseline vs each loosening;
  stop
}
@enduml
